<!--
  The XAML round deliberately keeps two pre-.NET 11 code paths alive:

    * XamlProbeRuntime  - inflated by the reflection-based XAML parser
    * XamlBindClassic   - bound through string paths resolved by reflection

  Both are exactly what full trimming is allowed to break (Microsoft documents
  compiled bindings as *required* under full trimming and NativeAOT), and this
  app builds with AndroidLinkMode=Full. Without rooting them the probes would
  either throw or, worse, quietly measure a degraded path.

  Scope is deliberately narrow: the probe namespace only. Nothing here changes
  what the rest of the app gets trimmed down to, so the round does not distort
  the size numbers of the other benchmarks.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="HorusStudio.Maui.MaterialDesignControls.Sample">
    <namespace fullname="HorusStudio.Maui.MaterialDesignControls.Sample.Benchmarks.XamlProbes" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
